      "title": "Untitled",
      "summary": "Biography\n            Craig McLuckie is a prominent figure in the tech industry, known for his significant contributions to cloud computing and open-source projects. He co-founded Kubernetes, an open-source container orchestration platform, and played a crucial role in launching Google Compute Engine. Additionally, he chaired the Cloud Native Computing Foundation and served as the VP of R&D at VMware. McLuckie's expertise spans various domains, including enterprise systems and cloud-native development, making him a key figure in modern computing practices.",
